# Line endings for the npm manifests, pinned to LF on checkout.
#
# npm does NOT always write lockfiles as LF. Measured with npm 11.6.2 on
# Windows: npm copies package.json's OWN newline style into the lockfile it
# writes. So with core.autocrlf=true, a CRLF package.json makes npm emit a
# CRLF package-lock.json, git normalizes it back to LF on commit, and the
# byte-identity check in test/lockfile-drift.test.mjs can never pass.
#
# Pinning BOTH files to eol=lf is the fix: package.json checks out LF, npm
# therefore writes LF, and the bytes on disk match the bytes git stores.
package.json text eol=lf
**/package.json text eol=lf
package-lock.json text eol=lf
**/package-lock.json text eol=lf
